  <h3>Academic Integrity Policy:</h3>
  <p><span data-field="academic_integrity_policy">Because of the opportunity for cheating, all students taking in-class problems or exams are REQUIRED to use Lockdown Browser and respondus monitor via a webcam. If you take your exams off the computer screen while doing these assignments you will be flagged and I will review the video. At the professor's discretion, flagged students may incur a penalty to their grade. The UTEP policy on academic integrity and scholastic dishonesty can be found at: <span data-field="utep_integrity_link">{{ academic_integrity_policy">Because of the opportunity for cheating, all students taking in-class problems or exams are REQUIRED to use Lockdown Browser and respondus monitor via a webcam. If you take your exams off the computer screen while doing these assignments you will be flagged and I will review the video. At the professor's discretion, flagged students may incur a penalty to their grade. The UTEP policy on academic integrity and scholastic dishonesty can be found at: <span data-field= }}</span>. All students will be expected to adhere to this policy.</span></p>

  <h3>Civility Statement:</h3>
  <p><span data-field="civility_statement">Students are expected to treat each other and the instructor with civility at all times during the brief time we meet each week. If an issue of an online class, please contact The Center for Academic Support and Services (CASS) at 747-5148, or by email to <span data-field="cass_email">{{ civility_statement">Students are expected to treat each other and the instructor with civility at all times during the brief time we meet each week. If an issue of an online class, please contact The Center for Academic Support and Services (CASS) at 747-5148, or by email to <span data-field= }}</span>, or visit their office located in UTEP Union East, Room 106. For additional information, please visit the CASS website at <span data-field="cass_website">{{ cass_website }}</span>. Requested accommodations must be made 3 working days before an examination. Students requesting accommodations must request a phone call meeting with the professor to discuss the details before they will be implemented, preferably at the beginning of the semester.</span></p>
